{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/fiedlerVector(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)-32sf7"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The Fiedler vector: λ₂ and a unit eigenvector of it, with the canonical sign (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"FiedlerVector","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); nil when the graph is not connected. NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"fiedler_vector","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/fiedlervector(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)-32sf7"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fiedlerVector"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":" = false, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"FiedlerVector","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">? "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At least two vertices, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"text":". Every weight is finite and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nonnegative, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":", when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" matrix–vector"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver answers and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached the default limits in the measurements."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Throws","type":"aside"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE13fiedlerVector6weight10normalized9tolerance13maxIterationsAD07FiedlerF0VyxGSgqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_SbSdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKSBRd__lF","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fiedlerVector","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"t